@@ -126,3 +126,22 @@ Android may kill the process when permission changes, so this recovery does not
 establish process-death persistence. The permission watcher is removed on destroy.
 
 `SubmittedNavigation` from `./submitted-navigation` owns submitted-address history, stale-check fencing and revision-bound explicit one-time overrides. Hosts validate/resolve addresses and supply a verdict check. Failed checks stay unavailable. Hosts retain warning/confirmation UI, sandbox configuration and all navigation authorization. This controller cannot observe internal iframe navigation or certify loaded content.
+
+## Android host web policy
+
+Hosts with a persistent and an ephemeral (private) browser profile share three pure-JVM
+policy classes in `ai.eliza.plugins.browsersurface` (no Android types; tested by
+`node --test test/native-host/web-policy.node.mjs`, which needs a JDK):
+
+- `BrowserWebOrigin`: canonical `scheme://host[:port]` for http(s) only (no user info,
+  control characters or over-long addresses), `blob:` owners, and "this site and its
+  subdomains" matching for Clear data for this site.
+- `BrowserDownloadPolicy`: a download carries the tab's cookie only for the exact origin of
+  that tab's committed page while the tab is open; `data:` files are decoded natively within
+  a 64 MB bound; file names are portable; the download list never persists ephemeral-profile
+  entries, forgets them when their tab closes, and is cleared by Clear browsing data and per site.
+- `BrowserSitePermissions`: camera, microphone and location decisions per exact origin for the
+  persistent profile only; ephemeral tabs never read or record one; bounded, revocable per site.
+
+The host keeps the review and permission UI, its wording, OS runtime permission requests,
+sealed storage of the permission snapshot and the OS download service.
